Criterion 5, second half: a deliberately broken golden must make the job red.

Method: fresh clone of origin/main, append invalid Dart to
tool/golden/stripped/lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart, then run the
bare --apply strip (which copies that golden into place) and analyze.

--- flutter analyze, exit 1 ---
  error • Invalid reference to 'this' expression • lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart:13:29 • invalid_reference_to_this
  error • Expected to find ';' • lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart:13:37 • expected_token
  error • The name 'not' isn't defined, so it can't be used in an 'is' expression. Try changing the name to the name of an existing type, or creating a type with the name 'not' • lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart:13:37 • type_test_with_undefined_name
  error • Undefined class 'valid'. Try changing the name to the name of an existing class, or creating a class with the name 'valid' • lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart:13:41 • undefined_class
  error • Expected to find ';' • lib/core/routing/routes_registry.dart:13:47 • expected_token

5 errors reported; analyze exit code 1, so the strip-smoke matrix job is RED.
This also answers criterion 7: excluding tool/golden/** from in-place
analysis does not hide breakage, because the matrix analyzes the golden
once it has been copied into the stripped tree.
